WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.970
Carmen Lopez can only imagine what the sea
looks like.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:21.770
But that hasn't stopped the 21 year old Spaniard
from riding the surf.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.470
I feel free and relaxed.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.340
I don't have any concerns and it's just me
and the wave.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.890
Coach Lucas Garcia guides Carmen by whistled
signals.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:40.280
He's trained her to compete at the World Adaptive
Surfing Championship.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.550
No one had ever thought that blind people
could surf.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.500
And suddenly we find Carmen, who can surf.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.230
She needs some extra help in the water compared
to other adapted sports, but at the end when

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:55.670
someone wants something, they can break the
limits and everyone can surf.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.579
Carmen was born with congenital glaucoma,
and lost her vision completely when she was

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:00.730
a child.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:06.080
She wants to encourage others with physical
challenges to push past their limits.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.270
To keep showing day by day and with everything
that I do on this, that if you want something

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.450
you can get it.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.860
And if you have or do not have a disability,
the important thing is to do what you like

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.860
the most.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.780
And that people put their own barriers up,
no one else puts them there.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.619
Carmen has also learned figure-skating and
horseback riding.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:28.530
With her bold attitude, the sea's the limit.

